  in order to overcome this of course the  obvious thing is to to lower the bar a  little bit in the sense that not you  saying useless stuff all the time but  that often you're very much  underestimating the actual value of the  things that you want to contribute so  maybe you feel like a thought that you  have is obvious to everyone else which  is why you don't need to share it but  very often the truth is that this  thought that you are having is not at  all obvious to at least some people in  the room which is why many more things  very likely are worth to be shared than  you might think and one little technique  that I find quite helpful here is with  what some people call the barrier of  silence and this is that often during  the course of a meeting the longer the  meeting continues without you having  said anything the harder it will be for  you to know suddenly after the meeting  is already one hour in  to only now start talking and start  saying something for the very first time  so this barrier of silence is building  up over time the longer the meeting gets  which is why a typical recommendation is  that you should try in the very  beginning just at the start of the  meeting to say something interact with  someone just drop a couple of comments  couple of remarks even if maybe they are  not the the most valuable ones ever but  if you do this then this barrier this  perceived hurdle for you to talk again  engage again will feel much lower much  more easy to overcome than if you  wouldn't have said anything for the very  first significant part of the meeting  next tip to succeed as an introvert is  to focus more on your strengths and of  course this now Taps into some cliches  and of course introverts are also  different and not every introvert  behaves in the same way but at least  some of the strengths that are typically  associated with introverts is active  listening that maybe you don't have the  need talk all the time yourself but  actually you're a really good listener  and you can detect perceive things while  just listening to someone that maybe  someone else who is a louder or who he  or she might be louder might not be able  to do this right so active listening  build on that obviously this is a very  very crucial skill in Professional  Services second empathy  here again what many people seem to  believe is that introverts are more  empathetic because they have these  antennas for the feelings for the  emotions of other people which are easy  maybe to be overheard if you just focus  too much on just talking yourself use  that empathy is so important so crucial  for Professional Services it is a  people's business this is a relationship  business and last but not least again  maybe a cliche but many people seem to  believe that introverts are also more  analytically inclined more analytically  able again of course this is a very  valuable skill in Consulting as well so  yes maybe you won't perform to the level  as other people do in some of the other  areas where the extroverts are stronger  but then just double down on your  strengths try to really excel in the  parts where you are good at and of  course you can then also get all the  positive evaluations all the fast pack  promotions and all these things you  might fancy also not right based on such  a virtues such strengths that you can  play all right and of course last but  not least what's really important then  to you is the weekends you need to  recharge your batteries at some point  very likely for money to Thursday Monday  to Friday you won't really have the  ability to do that at some point you  should just accept that if this is you  if this is your personality probably  Saturday and Sunday it will be very  challenging for you to now also then  just do lots of social things spend lots  of time with your friends go out in the  evenings I mean if this is a great for  you if this Fields like the right thing  to do for you of course feel free to do  that but for introverts I think for many  of us for me again included the week it  was often a time where I just slept in  where I just enjoyed a slower day and  rather not engaging too much with many  other people and at some point you might  need to accept that this is just what  you need to do in order to also properly  prepare yourself for then the next  rather busy and challenging week so this  is my thoughts on introverts please let  me know in the comments is this your  experience as well I would always be  very interested also in some suggestions  that you might have on how to deal with  this my my name is Heinrich thanks to  all the members of firm learning please  leave a like if you took any value out  of this subscribe if you like this type  of content and want to see more looking  forward to the next video next week and  bye
 

